{"repositoryId":783590608,"availability":"available","full":"diceroll123/pymermaider","name":"pymermaider","description":"A Python class diagram maker compatible with Mermaid.js (and GitHub), written in Rust.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":48,"forks":2,"created":"2024-04-08T07:35:50Z","updated":"2026-10-11T04:27:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://diceroll123.github.io/pymermaider/","topics":["mermaid-diagrams","mermaidjs","pyo3","python","ruff","rust","rustpython"],"demo":"https://diceroll123.github.io/pymermaider/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:27.424Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:27.424Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:27.424Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:38:27.424Z","stars":48,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Try the online pymermaider playground! powered by WebAssembly 🎉","pymermaider is a tool written in Rust designed to generate mermaid.js class diagrams from Python code. By analyzing Python code, pymermaider automatically generates mermaid.js-compatible diagrams that represent the class structures, including classes, methods, attributes, and their relationships. This tool aims to simplify the documentation process for Python projects, making it easier to visualize class hierarchies and relationships."],"features":["Automatic Class Diagram Generation: Generate detailed class diagrams from Python codebases with minimal configuration.","Mermaid.js Compatibility: Outputs diagrams in mermaid.js markdown syntax, ready to be embedded in your markdown documents or rendered using mermaid.js tools. GitHub supports this natively as you'll see below!","Classes, including nested classes (emitted as Outer.Inner ) and classes defined in functions","Attributes (annotated and simple assignments) and methods, including async, @classmethod, @staticmethod, @abstractmethod, @final, @overload and @override","@propert